course: dictionary
lesson: 7266
title: A journey with meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A pilgrimage is a journey, often a long one, to a place that matters deeply to the traveller. Most often the place is holy, and the trip is made for religious reasons. «Mansa Musa made his pilgrimage to Mecca in 1324» tells you he travelled to Mecca, a holy city, for his faith.
explain: The word can also mean a trip to a place that is very special to you, such as a writer's house or a sports ground. Use the clues around the word. If the sentence mentions faith, prayer or a holy city, it is the religious meaning. If it mentions a hero or a favourite place, it is the second meaning.
explain: «The Five Pillars are: the declaration of faith, prayer five times a day, giving to the poor, fasting in Ramadan and the pilgrimage to Mecca.» The list is about religious duties, so pilgrimage must mean a religious journey. Test your meaning by putting it in the sentence in place of the word and checking that it still makes sense.
fact: A pilgrimage is a journey to a place that is special to you, often for religious reasons.
fact: Mecca is a holy city for Muslims, and the pilgrimage to Mecca is called the Hajj.
fact: «Mansa Musa, ruler of the Mali Empire in West Africa, made his pilgrimage to Mecca in 1324.»
fact: Other holy places people travel to include Lourdes, Canterbury, Santiago and Jerusalem.
fact: A pilgrimage can also be a trip to a place that is special to you, such as a famous writer's house.
exercise: «Mansa Musa made his pilgrimage to Mecca in 1324.» What is a pilgrimage in this sentence? | *A long journey to a holy place for religious reasons | A journey to a holy place for religious reasons | A short trip to the shops for food | A race around the city
exercise: Lena visits the house of her favourite author and calls it a pilgrimage. What does she mean? | She is looking for a lost dog | *A trip to a place that is very special to her | She is ill and needs a doctor | She is angry with the author
exercise: In «Muslims live their faith every day through the Five Pillars and, if they can, making the pilgrimage to Mecca», which words show the pilgrimage is religious? | *Faith and the Five Pillars | Ramadan and gold | Every day and if they can | Making and Mecca
test: «Mansa Musa's pilgrimage to Mecca in 1324 carried so much gold that its price fell in Cairo.» What does pilgrimage mean here? | A market in Cairo | A ruler's gold mine | *A journey to Mecca for religious reasons | A holy journey to Mecca
test: Which sentence uses pilgrimage to mean a search for something good in life? | The football pitch was muddy. | The bus was late this morning. | She cooked dinner for her family. | *His long life was a pilgrimage to find kindness and truth.
exam: What is a pilgrimage? | A type of holiday food | A fast run around the park | A school trip to the museum | *A journey to a holy place or a place very special to you
</br>
